---
import SiteLayout from '@nyameko/ui/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="Getting started" siteName="Quantum Platform" section="User Portal"
  description="Register, secure your account, join a research programme and start using Workbench and Slurm.">
  <section class="section container start-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">START HERE · RESEARCH ACCESS</p>
    <h1>Your path from account to research</h1>
    <p class="lede">A guided first-day checklist for students, principal investigators and researchers. Account registration, resource approval and actual compute access are separate steps.</p>
    <div class="start-actions">
      <a href="/account/signup/" class="start-primary">Create account</a>
      <a href="/login/">Already registered? Sign in</a>
    </div>

    <nav class="quick-links" aria-label="Jump to getting-started topic">
      <a href="#secure">Security first</a><a href="#students">Students</a><a href="#pis">PIs</a>
      <a href="#resources">Resources</a><a href="#compute">Jupyter &amp; Slurm</a>
      <a href="#learning">Learn &amp; Guide</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="steps">
      <section id="secure" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Secure your research account before accessing machines</h2>
          <p>Verify your email address, complete your research profile, enable multi-factor authentication, and register <strong>only your public</strong> SSH and WireGuard keys. Do not upload private keys or recovery codes.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/profile/">Research profile</a><a href="/account/mfa/settings/">Set up MFA</a><a href="/account/access-keys/">SSH &amp; WireGuard keys</a></div>
          <p class="step-note">Key registration is a request for provisioning, not proof that a tunnel or SSH account is already active.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="students" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Student or existing research member? Request a programme membership</h2>
          <p>Sign in, complete your profile, visit Research Programmes and request membership in an existing programme. Your PI or programme administrator reviews it. A registered account alone has no GPU or QPU allocation.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/programmes/">Browse programmes</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="pis" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Principal investigator? Apply to lead a programme</h2>
          <p>Provide your institution, programme name and research description in the PI application. Your application is reviewed before a programme is approved and members can receive entitlements.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/programmes/apply/">Apply as a PI</a><a href="/programmes/">Application status</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="resources" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Check your resource entitlements</h2>
          <p>After programme and identity approval, verify which CPU, A100/H200 GPU or remote QPU resources are actually allocated. You must have the necessary environment and provider authorization before submitting a hardware workload.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/access/">View access</a><a href="/security/">Security and provisioning</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="compute" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">05</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Launch Workbench, then submit a small CPU Slurm job</h2>
          <p>Open Jupyter Workbench with your provisioned research identity. Begin with an available local notebook, then use Runs to submit an approved CPU reference workflow. Record its job ID, scheduler status and result manifest. A submitted job is not yet a completed result.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/workbench/">Jupyter Workbench</a><a href="/notebooks/">Notebooks</a><a href="/runs/">Slurm Runs</a></div>
          <p class="step-note">Using an SSH shell? Submit through the existing Slurm client (<code>sbatch</code>, <code>squeue</code>, <code>sacct</code>) after your account and scheduler allocation are ready. Interactive zsh is optional and does not change job shebangs.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="learning" class="start-step">
        <span class="step-number">06</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Continue your learning journey with Quantum Guide</h2>
          <p>Use Guide for explanations, research navigation and approved notebook references. It is not a substitute for executing and validating scientific code. Your conversations and permissions belong to the research account; terminal connections require explicit authentication.</p>
          <div class="step-links"><a href="/agent/">Open Guide</a><a href="https://github.com/nyameko/quantum-workflows/tree/main/labs">Open scientific labs on GitHub</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="help-note">
      <h2>Need help or waiting for approval?</h2>
      <p>Check your account security, programme membership and resource access status. If approval or provisioning is pending, don't generate repeated keys or job submissions. Contact your programme administrator through the approved support channel; never include passwords, tokens, private keys or recovery codes in support messages.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .start-page { max-width: 1000px; padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  h1 { margin: .5rem 0; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 4rem); letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .lede { max-width: 52rem; }
  .start-actions, .step-links, .quick-links { display:flex; gap:.75rem 1.1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; }
  .start-actions { margin: 1.6rem 0 2.2rem; }
  .start-actions a, .step-links a, .quick-links a { color: var(--purple); text-underline-offset: .2rem; }
  .start-actions a:focus-visible, .step-links a:focus-visible, .quick-links a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--purple); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .start-actions .start-primary { border-radius: .6rem; background: var(--purple-strong); color: white; padding: .7rem 1rem; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; }
  .quick-links { padding: 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: .8rem; }
  .steps { margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .start-step { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0,1fr); gap: 1.2rem; padding: 1.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .step-number { font-weight: 800; color: var(--purple); letter-spacing:.1em; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.25rem,2vw,1.55rem); margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .start-step p, .help-note p { line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted-strong); }
  .step-links { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .step-note { font-size: .9rem; }
  .help-note { margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:.85rem; }
  @media(max-width:600px){ .start-page{padding-top:2rem;} .start-step{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.3rem;} }
</style>
